.TH GITEXTENSIONS 1 "" "Git Extensions" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitextensions \- browse and manage Git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitextensions
.RI [ repository ]
.br
.B gitextensions --version
.br
.B gitextensions --help
.br
.B gitextensions --smoke-test
.RI [ repository ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git Extensions provides a graphical interface to Git. Pass a repository directory
to open it, or launch from the repository's working directory.
The application runs in an X11 desktop session, including XWayland.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version and exit without starting a graphical session.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Start the graphical application, verify that its window and repository load,
then exit automatically. A failure produces a nonzero exit status.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/lib/gitextensions/
contains the application and its bundled .NET runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/Azreal42/gitextensions/issues
